<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Random Joke</title>
<style>
    .joke {
        color: red;
    }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<button id="jokeButton">Show me a joke!</button>

<script>
// ... (same as before) 

jokeButton.addEventListener("click", function() {
    var randomJoke = jokes[Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length)];
    document.body.innerHTML = '<p class="joke">' + randomJoke + '</p>';
});
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

In this response, Assistant A uses a CSS class `.joke` to change the color of the joke text to red. The CSS class is applied to the paragraph element generated by the script (`<p class="joke">' + randomJoke + '</p>`).

